@* Rating's Overview, written by hand after Slider's: saving a rating (previewed in each mode),
   clearing it, showing one read-only, and states. Accessibility and See also come from the doc
   comment. *@

<TextBlock>A rating is a radio button for each star in a fieldset. It posts with the form, and hovering fills the stars up to the pointer. For a score on a longer scale, use a <Anchor Href="docs/components/slider">Slider</Anchor> or a <Anchor Href="docs/components/number-field">NumberField</Anchor>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Saving a rating</Heading>
<TextBlock>A rating binds to <Code>int</Code> or <Code>int?</Code>, from 1 to <Code>Max</Code> (5 by default). The value posts as a number with the form.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="rating-usage" />
<TextBlock>A form post can send any number, so check the range on the server, with <Code>[Range(1, 5)]</Code>. Before trusting a posted value, see <Anchor Href="docs/common/forms#values-a-form-post-can-change">Values a form post can change</Anchor>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Clearing a rating</Heading>
<TextBlock>Bound to <Code>int?</Code>, a rating can be empty. Clicking the chosen star clears it, and the arrow keys reach "No rating" before the first star, which screen readers announce. A required rating has no empty choice, as a checked radio would count as an answer.</TextBlock>
<TextBlock>Bound to <Code>int</Code>, a rating starts with no star chosen when the value is 0, and can't be cleared once one is.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Showing a rating</Heading>
<TextBlock>To show a rating someone can't change, such as an average, set <Code>ReadOnly</Code>. It takes any number, <Code>double</Code> too, and fills the stars to the exact fraction: 4.3 fills 86%.</TextBlock>
<TextBlock><Code>Icon</Code> changes the star, <Code>Accent</Code> its color, and <Code>Max</Code> how many there are.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="rating-display" />
<TextBlock>Screen readers hear one image, "4.3 out of 5 stars". In a <Anchor Href="docs/components/form">Form</Anchor>, a read-only rating posts its value.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Sizes and disabled</Heading>
<TextBlock>To line a rating up with other fields, set <Code>Size</Code>. A <Code>Disabled</Code> rating can't be changed and doesn't post. In a read-only Form, a rating shows as a display.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Labels and localization</Heading>
<TextBlock>The names screen readers hear for the stars come from the app's text. To set them for the whole app, see <Anchor Href="docs/common/text">Text and other languages</Anchor>.</TextBlock>
<Prose Class="site-table ib-scroll">
    <table>
        <thead><tr><th>IzzyText</th><th>Sets</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td><Code>RatingOneStar</Code></td><td>The first star's name</td><td>"1 star"</td></tr>
            <tr><td><Code>RatingStars</Code></td><td>The other stars' names; <Code>{0}</Code> is the number</td><td>"{0} stars"</td></tr>
            <tr><td><Code>RatingNone</Code></td><td>The empty choice's name</td><td>"No rating"</td></tr>
            <tr><td><Code>RatingOutOf</Code></td><td>A read-only rating's name; <Code>{0}</Code> is the value, <Code>{1}</Code> the number of stars</td><td>"{0} out of {1} stars"</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</Prose>

